/target
# Matches `<repo>/mock/target/` AND any nested
# `<crate>/mock/target/` produced by test fixtures that invoke
# `cargo mock install` against a tempdir-shaped path. The `**/`
# prefix is required: a bare `mock/target/` pattern with an
# internal slash is anchored to the gitignore's own directory by
# git's fnmatch FNM_PATHNAME semantics, so it would not match
# nested copies under `mock/crates/<name>/mock/target/`.
**/mock/target/
/mock/Cargo.lock
# The lint cdylib pack is its own workspace root (excluded from the tool
# workspace); its build dir and lock live beside its manifest.
/mock/crates/mockspace-builtin-lints/target/
/mock/crates/mockspace-builtin-lints/Cargo.lock
.DS_Store
# spotlight marker the per-agent worktrees carry; never part of a tree.
.metadata_never_index
*.swp
*.swo
*.rs.bk

# === mockspace-managed build artifacts (do not edit) ===
# Catch-all: every cargo build dir, including nested ones under benches/,
# tests/, and research sketches. A leading-slash /target would miss those.
target/
# === end mockspace-managed build artifacts ===

# The desktop indexer's opt-out marker. Every per-agent worktree gets one on
# creation, per the workspace's worktree rule, because a build tree nobody
# marked is a few thousand files for the indexer per run. It is a property of
# the checkout rather than of the project, so it is ignored rather than
# committed, and without this line every worktree spawned here starts dirty.
.metadata_never_index
